{"name":"Macau","hex":"#46c299","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Macau","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, special administrative region, and peninsula in China, west of Hong Kong.","a former Portuguese colony in modern southern China between 1557 and 1999."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Macau"}],"entries":[{"title":"Macau","blocks":[{"text":"Macau or Macao is a special administrative region of China. It consists of the Macau Peninsula, the islands of Taipa and Coloane, the Cotai reclamation zone between Taipa and Coloane, and several smaller islets. It borders Zhuhai to the north and west, and it lies west of Hong Kong, separated by the Pearl River estuary. With a population of about 720,000 people and a land area of 32.9 square kilometres (12.7 sq mi), it is the most densely populated region in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Flag_of_Macau.svg/330px-Flag_of_Macau.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macau","wikidata":"Q14773"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Nieuhof-Ambassade-vers-la-Chine-1665_0739.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dutch ships firing their cannons in the waters of Macau, drawn in 1665","link":"https://en.wik